1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:03,480
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,880
(Episode 51)

5
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:11,180
Why are you giving your card
to this stranger?

6
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:12,720
Can't you tell
just by looking at him?

7
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,120
He's a con artist.

8
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:16,690
Get off me!

9
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:18,960
- What do you think you're doing?
- Darn it.

10
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,830
See? What did I tell you?
I told you he was a creep.

11
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,960
Let's get out of here.

12
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:42,880
Get off me!

13
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:45,250
What do you think you're doing?

14
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:50,860
That was definitely
a mosquito bite scar.

15
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:55,490
It's a condition that's run
in our family for generations.

16
00:00:56,430 --> 00:00:57,730
Every time we get a mosquito bite,

17
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:59,300
we end up scratching it
for three days straight,

18
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,170
taking antibiotics,
and barely healing.

19
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:08,370
That young woman must have
the exact same condition.

20
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:12,540
(Kang Hae Ra,
Design Team Leader at Cheongma)

21
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:13,980
("I'll become a designer
worthy of Cheongma's name")

22
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:16,450
Her temper was just like
Ae Sook's, too.

23
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:26,060
Could they really
be connected somehow?

24
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:35,230
That total weirdo
ruined my digestion.

25
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:37,700
How was he a weirdo?

26
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,770
He brought dry cleaning money
in case he ruined your clothes.

27
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:44,210
You've got to stop judging people
solely by how they look.

28
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:45,780
Couldn't you just tell?

29
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,980
He practically screams fraud
from a mile away.

30
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:51,380
Besides, his face
just gives me bad vibes.

31
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:53,380
You should steer clear
of people like that right away.

32
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,590
Unbelievable.

33
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,920
Wait.

34
00:01:56,990 --> 00:01:58,790
You gave him your business card,
didn't you?

35
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,090
- Yes.
- Why did you do that?

36
00:02:01,090 --> 00:02:04,100
It has your phone number
and your department on it.

37
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:06,000
How could you just hand it out
so carelessly?

38
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,930
Nothing is going to happen
from a single business card.

39
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,200
You worry about
the most pointless things.

40
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:10,970
You never know.

41
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:13,070
What if he clings to you
and gives you a hard time?

42
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:15,840
Could he be any worse than you?

43
00:02:16,570 --> 00:02:17,580
What did I do?

44
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:29,520
The truth is,
I think Attorney Seo died...

45
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:31,920
while trying to help Eun Seol.

46
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,590
From what I heard,

47
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:36,130
it seems Attorney Seo
liked Eun Seol a lot.

48
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,560
Eun Seol appreciated him,

49
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,870
but she never thought of him
in a romantic way.

50
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,240
What brings you here?

51
00:02:53,010 --> 00:02:54,080
Well...

52
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:57,550
I felt like we needed to talk.

53
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:00,020
Do you have a minute?

54
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:01,750
Yes, please come in.

55
00:03:03,690 --> 00:03:04,690
Well...

56
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,890
I heard about it from Eun Guk.

57
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:08,890
You must've been really upset.

58
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,430
If I were in your shoes,

59
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,600
it would've been hard
to watch my family...

60
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,540
from so close.

61
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:22,410
I can only imagine...

62
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:26,210
how painful it must've been for you.

63
00:03:27,610 --> 00:03:29,550
But you know...

64
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,020
Eun Guk...

65
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:36,450
truly cares about you a lot.

66
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,220
Honestly, I was worried
deep down, too.

67
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:42,890
I was worried he'd be reckless...

68
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,160
and pursue you,

69
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,670
only to hurt your feelings
in the end.

70
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:55,040
But that boy...

71
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:57,580
He's sincere.

72
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,080
That's why...

73
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:02,110
I told you to move out
before things got out of hand.

74
00:04:02,950 --> 00:04:03,980
And then...

75
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:06,380
there's Eun Seol.

76
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,790
What are you doing?
Please don't do this.

77
00:04:14,290 --> 00:04:15,290
No, let me.

78
00:04:16,330 --> 00:04:19,560
Attorney Seo was attacked
while helping our Eun Seol.

79
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:21,530
As her father,

80
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:24,770
I'll get on my knees a million,
even ten million times.

81
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,640
It's not like doing this
will bring Hyun Jae back.

82
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:29,170
Please stop.

83
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:33,210
I am truly sorry.

84
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:37,720
I'll never forget
his heartfelt efforts...

85
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:41,020
and how hard he tried
to clear Eun Seol's name.

86
00:04:43,050 --> 00:04:44,290
I told you to get up.

87
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:46,990
Teun Teun's mom.

88
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:50,260
This time, we'll see to it...

89
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,430
that Attorney Seo gets justice.

90
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:55,370
So,

91
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:57,800
please give us a chance
just this once.

92
00:05:00,570 --> 00:05:02,610
Good intentions aren't enough
to get things done.

93
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:05,210
Still, we can't just sit back
and do nothing.

94
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,010
We have to at least try.

95
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:09,780
We'll help you, Teun Teun's mom.

96
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:18,320
So I guess
I'll be alone this weekend.

97
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:22,860
You said you wanted
to be alone sometimes.

98
00:05:23,290 --> 00:05:25,730
Still, now that
I'll actually be alone,

99
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:28,170
I feel a bit lonely for some reason.

100
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:33,500
Why don't we go on a trip too?

101
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:36,210
Once you get back from spending
the weekend with CEO Park,

102
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:37,910
why don't we leave next week?

103
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,510
Well, next week,

104
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:44,880
I have to inspect
the department store food hall.

105
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,880
We can go after that.

106
00:05:46,950 --> 00:05:49,890
A tight schedule just wears you out.

107
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:52,290
Next time, let's take Hae Ra
and go together.

108
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,560
Chief Cha as well.

109
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:56,790
Director Joo, you should clear
your schedule in advance too.

110
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,530
Sure, just let me know in advance,

111
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:02,230
and I'll handle
all the hotel bookings.

112
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,110
Where do you stand on Director Joo?

113
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:12,040
What do you mean, where do I stand?

114
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:15,010
I just think of her
as a valued employee.

115
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:17,750
Right, Director Joo is an employee.

116
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,850
No matter
how much like family we are,

117
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:23,150
including her on a family trip
is crossing the line.

118
00:06:23,490 --> 00:06:26,690
Come on, why are you suddenly
making a big deal out of this?

119
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:29,730
You two are always attached
at the hip like real sisters.

120
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,730
That may be so,

121
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,870
but I'd rather you didn't do this
from now on.

122
00:06:35,630 --> 00:06:36,900
Think about it.

123
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,240
When you treat a subordinate
like family,

124
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:42,170
they can sometimes get confused
about their place.

125
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:45,280
Does Director Joo seem like
that kind of person to you?

126
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:49,280
She doesn't yet,
so let's be careful from now on.

127
00:06:57,290 --> 00:06:58,690
I'm home.

128
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:01,760
Mr. Seok Jin, you're back.

129
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:05,160
Are you making bookmarks
this year too?

130
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,800
Yes. Right outside
the apartment building,

131
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,670
the ginkgo and maple trees
have turned...

132
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:13,600
such gorgeous yellows and reds.

133
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,040
Who are you making all these for?

134
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,710
Well, you, of course.

135
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,780
Then, one for Hae Ra's mother,

136
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:23,080
and one for the nice lady.

137
00:07:24,050 --> 00:07:25,620
What about Hae Ra?
Aren't you giving her one?

138
00:07:27,850 --> 00:07:28,850
Hae Ra?

139
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,920
She'll pout if I don't
give her one, right?

140
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,490
Of course.

141
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:37,130
She was so hurt today,
thinking you hated her, Mom.

142
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:42,200
That's odd.
Hae Ra wouldn't be upset over that.

143
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:45,340
Also, tomorrow,

144
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,670
you know we're going to the hospital
with Director Joo, right?

145
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:49,770
Yes.

146
00:07:50,270 --> 00:07:51,340
At the hospital tomorrow,

147
00:07:51,710 --> 00:07:53,680
let's listen carefully
to what the doctor says.

148
00:07:54,250 --> 00:07:56,980
If you cooperate with the doctor,
I'll get you a gift.

149
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:58,380
What do you want, Mom?

150
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:01,290
There isn't anything I want,

151
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:05,660
but that Cinderella show
I told you about last time...

152
00:08:05,990 --> 00:08:07,330
I really want to see that.

153
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:10,600
Mom,

154
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:13,930
why don't we go watch that show
with Hae Ra?

155
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:17,970
Wait. With Hae Ra?

156
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:19,100
Yes.

157
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:21,740
Hae Ra seems like...

158
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:25,210
the wicked stepsister
from "Cinderella."

159
00:08:30,110 --> 00:08:32,650
Is there anything
you want to know about me?

160
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,250
About you, Eun Seol?

161
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:44,200
Not really.

162
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:54,170
Why is she denying me like this?

163
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,310
Could there be another reason?

164
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:03,410
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable. Please leave...

165
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,350
Just wait for now.

166
00:09:05,650 --> 00:09:07,180
It's not like
this is the first time.

167
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:08,850
We'll wait a bit,

168
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,820
but if anything seems off,
we're going to the police.

169
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:12,220
I'm getting a bad feeling this time.

170
00:09:28,470 --> 00:09:32,480
I shouldn't have followed
that old man Choi.

171
00:09:33,310 --> 00:09:36,310
I only went along
because he promised me a huge payout.

172
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:39,550
How was I supposed to know
it was a den of card sharks?

173
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,390
You stupid idiot!

174
00:09:47,990 --> 00:09:49,460
(Son)

175
00:09:58,100 --> 00:09:59,340
(15 missed calls: Son)

176
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:05,440
Your mom's alive. Don't worry.

177
00:10:10,410 --> 00:10:11,480
Good morning.

178
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:13,650
Good morning to you too, Eun Seol.

179
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,960
It's chilly in the mornings
and evenings.

180
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:20,060
You should've dressed warmer.

181
00:10:21,190 --> 00:10:22,930
It's still warm indoors, you know.

182
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:25,730
Weather like this makes it easier
to catch a cold.

183
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:27,400
Do you have a scarf or something?

184
00:10:36,110 --> 00:10:37,710
(Your mom's alive. Don't worry.)

185
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:45,380
The call cannot be connected.
You'll be transferred to voicemail.

186
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:47,590
You will be charged after the beep.

187
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:54,130
Wait, did she lose all her money
playing cards again?

188
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,230
No.

189
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,630
She hasn't got any money
to play with anyway.

190
00:11:01,470 --> 00:11:02,470
Don't tell me...

191
00:11:10,910 --> 00:11:12,080
Are you kidding me?

192
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:14,250
That old woman...

193
00:11:21,150 --> 00:11:22,720
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

194
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,320
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

195
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:31,060
You were friends with my mom.

196
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:35,130
I was curious about your life story.

197
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:38,700
She's not the type
to just be curious about me.

198
00:11:39,270 --> 00:11:42,870
She's definitely trying
to dig something up.

199
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:52,320
Here's the list of hospitals
to commit An Guk Cheol to.

200
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:55,420
I organized them
by distance from Seoul.

201
00:11:57,190 --> 00:11:58,260
Good work.

202
00:11:58,290 --> 00:12:01,460
The documents we prepared will work
at all these places, right?

203
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:05,000
Yes, I have finished coordinating
with the experts in this field.

204
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:08,230
All right. Report back
once preparations are complete.

205
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:10,370
And one more thing.

206
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:14,340
I think Ko Eun Seol
is looking into my background.

207
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:19,910
I haven't noticed anything
to suggest that, though.

208
00:12:21,410 --> 00:12:24,520
How can you be so sure,
Secretary Choi?

209
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:28,790
It's just what I gathered
while watching her carefully.

210
00:12:30,650 --> 00:12:33,120
My gut is far more accurate...

211
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,690
than what your two eyes have seen.

212
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,200
Also,

213
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,630
you seem to keep forgetting this,

214
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,300
but you ended Team Leader Seo
with your own hands.

215
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:51,410
Who's taking Team Leader Seo's death
the hardest right now?

216
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:56,110
If Ko Eun Seol digs into
Team Leader Seo's case,

217
00:12:56,110 --> 00:12:58,020
who'll be in the most danger?

218
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:05,160
Jun Hwan.

219
00:13:06,690 --> 00:13:09,190
Let's stay on our toes. Okay?

220
00:13:10,730 --> 00:13:11,730
Yes, ma'am.

221
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:14,670
I'll keep a close eye
on Ko Eun Seol.

222
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:33,620
There's no market trend
or marketing analysis data.

223
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:37,720
I noted at the bottom
that I'd submit that...

224
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:40,120
after getting a proper grasp
of the field.

225
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:44,500
Rather than sitting at a desk
analyzing numbers,

226
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,360
I thought working at the store...

227
00:13:46,430 --> 00:13:48,730
would give us
a more accurate analysis.

228
00:13:49,730 --> 00:13:53,200
These are all materials analyzed
by marketing experts.

229
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:56,140
Do you really think you can be
more accurate than them?

230
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:58,180
Data and field experience
are two different things.

231
00:13:58,710 --> 00:14:01,410
Isn't the customer feedback
we see and hear firsthand...

232
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:03,210
what we actually need?

233
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:05,920
When did you say you'd be going
for the on-site monitoring?

234
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:07,990
I plan to go next week.

235
00:14:08,590 --> 00:14:09,590
Sounds good.

236
00:14:09,590 --> 00:14:12,760
Then let's finalize the proposal
after the monitoring is done.

237
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:16,960
A customer satisfaction survey
will also be conducted that day.

238
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,330
I'll go support
the on-site work as well.

239
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:21,200
Then I'll be there that day as well.

240
00:14:22,430 --> 00:14:24,300
- Great work, everyone.
- Great work.

241
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,210
Ko Eun Seol.

242
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:32,810
This is the budget
for the scholarship program promo video.

243
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:34,580
Deliver it to Director Joo.

244
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:38,520
What? Are you saying no?

245
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,990
Of course not. I'll take it to her.

246
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:04,480
Eun Seol, do you have
something to say to me?

247
00:15:05,310 --> 00:15:06,340
No, ma'am.

248
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,250
The look in your eyes says you do.

249
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:12,080
Once I'm a little more certain,

250
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,790
I'll tell you.

251
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:18,420
Sure. I'll wait then.

252
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,660
Just what is she waiting
to be more certain about?

253
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:33,900
I'll look forward
to the promotional video.

254
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:36,110
Right. Then...

255
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:37,980
Eun Seol.

256
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,080
Would you like to come
with me this weekend...

257
00:15:44,150 --> 00:15:45,780
to Hee Jung's columbarium?

258
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:47,520
Let's get some fresh air
while we're at it.

259
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:52,020
No, thank you. I don't think
I'll have time this weekend.

260
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,860
I see. Guess I can't help it then.

261
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,030
Let's go together next time.

262
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:58,700
Sure.

263
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:21,650
Who is it?

264
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:24,920
Mom, I'm home.

265
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:29,090
- You're already back?
- Yes.

266
00:16:29,390 --> 00:16:31,430
Uncle picked me up today.

267
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:34,230
Uncle Hyun Jae went
on a business trip far away.

268
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:37,370
So Uncle Jokbal picked me up
instead today.

269
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:42,070
Teun Teun, finish your snack quickly
so we can go play soccer together.

270
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,870
I'll just put my bag down
and be right out.

271
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:50,150
Are you ignoring what I told you?

272
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:51,620
No.

273
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:53,680
Why would I ignore
what you said, boss?

274
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:57,020
I just came over to play
as Teun Teun's uncle.

275
00:16:58,690 --> 00:16:59,690
Don't tell me...

276
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,860
you're getting the wrong idea.

277
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:04,030
What wrong idea?

278
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:06,560
Maybe you think
I came here to see you...

279
00:17:06,630 --> 00:17:08,900
as a boyfriend or something.

280
00:17:08,970 --> 00:17:10,030
Look here, Eun Guk.

281
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:13,100
Can you hurry with the snacks?

282
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:15,910
I promised Teun Teun we'd go
to the field and play soccer today.

283
00:17:16,510 --> 00:17:18,510
If we don't hurry,
other people will take the goals.

284
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:21,250
- Come on.
- Just a minute.

285
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:27,280
Don't get the wrong idea,
and hurry up with our snacks.

286
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,750
Teun Teun said he was really hungry.

287
00:17:29,850 --> 00:17:32,090
- Come on, hurry.
- All right. Just let go of me.

288
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:34,190
Please make something delicious.

289
00:17:40,930 --> 00:17:43,730
My mother's checkup will probably
take about ten more minutes.

290
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:45,040
Okay.

291
00:17:45,970 --> 00:17:47,840
Chief Cha, you're truly admirable.

292
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,340
How many years has it been already,

293
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:51,410
taking care
of So Yeon's checkups like this?

294
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:53,980
As a mother,
she must feel so reassured.

295
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:57,080
I am all she has,

296
00:17:58,450 --> 00:17:59,580
and she is all I have.

297
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:04,920
I guess that's why
people raise children.

298
00:18:06,690 --> 00:18:09,130
I envy how close you two are.

299
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:15,870
Thank you for making time
to come today.

300
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:18,770
Well, it was the CEO's idea.

301
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,610
By the way...

302
00:18:22,770 --> 00:18:24,140
Earlier in the examination room,

303
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:27,480
didn't you ask
about So Yeon's memory?

304
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,880
Yes.

305
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:33,250
Lately, my mother has been
bringing up the past quite often.

306
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:37,990
She seems confused herself about
whether her memories are accurate.

307
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,260
What kind of memories?

308
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:45,600
Like CEO Kang and my father
not getting along,

309
00:18:46,430 --> 00:18:49,070
or CEO Kang being
a scary, bad person.

310
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:53,040
The doctor said...

311
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:57,170
memories that suddenly resurface
aren't always accurate,

312
00:18:57,740 --> 00:19:00,010
so we shouldn't believe
every single detail.

313
00:19:02,450 --> 00:19:04,150
Right, of course.

314
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:08,690
Even people like us
often mix up old memories.

315
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:16,630
Thank you for accompanying So Yeon
to the hospital today, Director Joo.

316
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:18,700
Don't mention it, sir.

317
00:19:19,630 --> 00:19:21,270
She's uncomfortable with me,
her daughter-in-law,

318
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:22,530
yet fine with Director Joo.

319
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:25,540
I want to like that woman,
but I really can't.

320
00:19:25,940 --> 00:19:27,470
Why does she hate me so much?

321
00:19:30,510 --> 00:19:33,080
"Like that woman?"

322
00:19:34,010 --> 00:19:37,280
That's not how a daughter-in-law
should speak about an elder.

323
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,620
You need to show So Yeon respect
as your mother-in-law.

324
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:43,620
Only then will she accept you
as her daughter-in-law.

325
00:19:44,290 --> 00:19:46,190
I know. You're right, Dad.

326
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:49,230
But she isn't
your typical mother-in-law.

327
00:19:49,490 --> 00:19:51,500
Her mental age doesn't
even seem like it's ten.

328
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:52,660
What can you do?

329
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:54,300
You brought this on yourself.

330
00:19:55,430 --> 00:19:56,430
Anyway, Director Joo.

331
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,340
About So Yeon.

332
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:01,040
Did you say she occasionally
brings up the past?

333
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:04,810
Yes. Her memory
hasn't fully returned.

334
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:08,250
From time to time,
she seems to recall false memories.

335
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:11,150
It gives me chills sometimes.

336
00:20:11,550 --> 00:20:13,950
She suddenly blurts out things
that kill the mood.

337
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:17,190
I just wish she'd stay quiet
at my engagement party.

338
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:18,760
Seriously?

339
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:21,790
Should we...

340
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,030
look into a nursing home
for her, then?

341
00:20:24,130 --> 00:20:25,130
Exactly.

342
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:27,260
Somewhere quiet with fresh air
would be great.

343
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,200
I'm all for it.

344
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:31,700
Chief Cha won't stand by
and let that happen.

345
00:20:32,170 --> 00:20:34,000
You should quietly observe for now,

346
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:37,570
and carefully bring up
a nursing home after the wedding.

347
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:39,910
Right. I just hope...

348
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:43,150
So Yeon holds it together
without any trouble until then.

349
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:04,800
Mom?

350
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:21,750
Mom!

351
00:21:24,390 --> 00:21:26,520
I never dwell on the past.

352
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,990
There's no point
in being bound by it.

353
00:21:29,090 --> 00:21:30,530
It just gets in the way.

354
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:33,560
I don't really have a past
worth mentioning.

355
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:37,470
I've just worked nonstop
since graduation.

356
00:21:38,270 --> 00:21:40,640
In a way, it has been an easy life.

357
00:21:42,070 --> 00:21:44,210
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

358
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:52,250
Mom.

359
00:21:54,050 --> 00:21:56,020
Is this why you hid everything?

360
00:21:58,690 --> 00:22:00,220
Were you afraid that I'd get hurt?

361
00:22:12,970 --> 00:22:14,670
You didn't forget
about tomorrow, right?

362
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:16,770
I'll be waiting there for you.

363
00:22:18,510 --> 00:22:19,710
I'll make sure not to be late.

364
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,080
Good.

365
00:22:22,610 --> 00:22:23,610
Well, then.

366
00:22:29,090 --> 00:22:30,090
Good night.

367
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,400
Sit down over here.

368
00:22:54,010 --> 00:22:56,580
(Part-time Job Plan)

369
00:22:57,250 --> 00:22:58,350
What's all this?

370
00:22:58,950 --> 00:23:00,050
What do you think?

371
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:02,190
No matter what,
we have to earn back...

372
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:04,790
the moving expenses
that Teun Teun's mom gave us.

373
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:06,260
So...

374
00:23:07,190 --> 00:23:09,660
you want me to work all these jobs?

375
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:11,430
Yes, get to work.

376
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:15,930
How can I do all this at my age?

377
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:18,100
Just because I spent a little money,

378
00:23:18,340 --> 00:23:20,540
you want to work your mother
to death?

379
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:21,740
What?

380
00:23:21,910 --> 00:23:22,910
A little?

381
00:23:25,610 --> 00:23:27,980
I'm the one working myself
to death here.

382
00:23:29,050 --> 00:23:30,680
You really have some nerve.

383
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:33,380
How could you lose all that money
playing cards?

384
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:35,720
That's gambling.

385
00:23:36,150 --> 00:23:38,890
Do you want to spend
your final years behind bars?

386
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:42,960
Old man Choi told me
he'd score me a big win,

387
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:45,230
so I tagged along,

388
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:50,170
but there were all these huge men
swarming around like wild dogs.

389
00:23:50,770 --> 00:23:52,370
I was so terrified.

390
00:23:53,070 --> 00:23:56,910
I ended up pouring in
every cent I had.

391
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,280
My money...

392
00:24:00,010 --> 00:24:02,750
My precious money. What do I do?

393
00:24:02,750 --> 00:24:04,480
How was that ever your money?

394
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,480
Stop crying!

395
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,520
The money is one thing,

396
00:24:09,090 --> 00:24:10,190
but this will make sure...

397
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,320
you don't even think about
playing cards again.

398
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:14,320
Get moving.

399
00:24:17,290 --> 00:24:19,400
- What do I do?
- Get up.

400
00:24:20,060 --> 00:24:22,300
Just sell me off already!

401
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:54,560
No...

402
00:25:01,470 --> 00:25:02,470
Thank you.

403
00:25:18,390 --> 00:25:19,490
Sorry, Mom.

404
00:25:21,090 --> 00:25:23,330
I've been so busy lately
that I couldn't visit often.

405
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,900
It must've been agonizing
to hold all that in.

406
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:47,720
Mom...

407
00:25:52,290 --> 00:25:53,660
I found out everything.

408
00:25:56,760 --> 00:25:59,200
What you were trying to hide.

409
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:11,310
It must've been so hard on you, Mom.

410
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:20,820
Mom...

411
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:25,620
Can't I just...

412
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:30,830
Can't I just stay your daughter?

413
00:26:36,870 --> 00:26:38,840
I just want to stay
as your daughter.

414
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,970
I won't look for anyone anymore.

415
00:27:01,690 --> 00:27:03,130
I've arrived.

416
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,670
I'm about to head out, too.

417
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:28,080
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

418
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:33,220
Eun Seol, do you have
something to say to me?

419
00:27:34,090 --> 00:27:35,630
Once I'm a little more certain,

420
00:27:36,860 --> 00:27:38,160
I'll tell you.

421
00:27:41,730 --> 00:27:44,870
No, this isn't the time
for a romantic getaway.

422
00:27:46,300 --> 00:27:50,240
Seo Hyun Jae caught me off guard
and blindsided me.

423
00:27:51,610 --> 00:27:55,010
Ko Eun Seol must definitely
be planning something right now.

424
00:28:02,950 --> 00:28:05,460
Well, look who it is.
If it isn't Ae Sook.

425
00:28:06,560 --> 00:28:08,960
Director, have you been doing well?

426
00:28:09,730 --> 00:28:11,160
It's the same as always here.

427
00:28:12,260 --> 00:28:16,230
Oh, right. I was actually
just about to call you.

428
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,970
Why? Did something happen?

429
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:21,240
Someone asked about you
a few days ago.

430
00:28:21,770 --> 00:28:23,440
She didn't say who she was,

431
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:25,680
but it was a young woman's voice.

432
00:28:26,910 --> 00:28:30,280
I told her I couldn't give out
personal information.

433
00:28:30,780 --> 00:28:32,580
You got her number, right?

434
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:34,580
Of course.

435
00:28:36,250 --> 00:28:38,760
Hello, Yeongsu High School
administration office.

436
00:28:39,690 --> 00:28:42,190
Hello, I have a quick question.

437
00:28:43,230 --> 00:28:44,690
Did someone call recently...

438
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:48,530
to ask about a former student
named Joo Ae Sook?

439
00:28:49,830 --> 00:28:50,970
Yes, someone did.

440
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:54,770
A woman asked about Joo Ae Sook.

441
00:28:55,310 --> 00:28:57,770
A lawyer had also come by
before that.

442
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:03,610
Then, among the graduates,

443
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:05,180
was there anyone
named Joo Ae Sook...

444
00:29:05,850 --> 00:29:08,890
So I told them
there was only one Joo Ae Sook...

445
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:11,420
among the students
enrolled that year.

446
00:29:14,620 --> 00:29:16,890
I see. Thank you for your help.

447
00:29:22,130 --> 00:29:23,500
Did that brat Ko Eun Seol...

448
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:27,470
even figure out
I grew up in an orphanage?

449
00:29:38,050 --> 00:29:39,250
Manager Na Tae Hoon...

450
00:29:40,080 --> 00:29:42,050
left this gift for you.

451
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:52,000
Then,

452
00:29:52,460 --> 00:29:54,460
did she find
what was in the box, too?

453
00:29:55,970 --> 00:29:58,230
Wait, even the recording?

454
00:29:59,340 --> 00:30:01,240
No. There's no way.

455
00:30:01,370 --> 00:30:02,710
Had she found it,

456
00:30:03,310 --> 00:30:05,110
she would've confronted me
immediately.

457
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:09,880
I have to do something...

458
00:30:10,310 --> 00:30:11,880
before she finds it.

459
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:27,960
Right.

460
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:30,730
Now that it's come to this,

461
00:30:31,330 --> 00:30:33,500
let's just say
I gave birth to Ko Eun Seol.

462
00:30:33,570 --> 00:30:35,000
(Maternity Handbook)

463
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:37,610
If I claim I'm her birth mother,

464
00:30:38,110 --> 00:30:39,540
what can she really do?

465
00:31:04,970 --> 00:31:06,800
- Yes?
- Eun Seol,

466
00:31:07,300 --> 00:31:08,610
where are you right now?

467
00:31:11,940 --> 00:31:14,980
I really need to meet with you
right away.

468
00:31:15,650 --> 00:31:17,550
I'll come to where you are.

469
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:09,500
Eun Seol,

470
00:32:10,670 --> 00:32:12,000
I made you wait, didn't I?

471
00:32:44,270 --> 00:32:48,170
(A Trap Called Desire)

472
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:52,010
Who did you go on this trip with?
I asked who you went with.

473
00:32:52,180 --> 00:32:55,080
Director Joo,
what are we to each other?

474
00:32:55,410 --> 00:32:56,410
Watch yourself.

475
00:32:56,410 --> 00:32:58,150
If you keep asking only
for Ko Eun Seol,

476
00:32:58,350 --> 00:32:59,480
I'll make you pay.

477
00:32:59,620 --> 00:33:02,120
Seok Jin, maybe we should look
for a nursing home.

478
00:33:02,120 --> 00:33:05,390
Mom wouldn't have done that.

479
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:08,960
I wonder what made
my daughter so curious.

480
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:11,430
Why now, of all times?

481
00:33:11,430 --> 00:33:14,960
Why come looking for me only now?

482
00:33:15,230 --> 00:33:17,530
Why? Is it because
I've been digging into your past?

483
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:20,200
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
